# Ford Sierra Mk1 five-door hatchback, 1982-1987.
#
# The aerodynamic Sierra that replaced the Cortina in September 1982: 4,367 mm
# long, 1,723 mm wide, 1,361 mm high, 2,603 mm wheelbase (estate 4,511 mm).
# 1.3-2.8 petrol and 2.3 diesel; XR4i from 1983, RS Cosworth from 1986.
# The comfort calibration anchor for the 1980s family car.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Sierra
#
# Colours: Rosso Red, Diamond White, Strato Silver and Cosmos Blue are documented
# Ford colours of the period.
#
# Weight: 400 in total (red 110, white 110, silver 90, blue 90), a top-five UK
# seller of the mid-1980s.
#
# Speed 190 km/h; comfort 120/510 (anchor). Classes 0,1,2.
# Dates: 1982-1987 with a road tail to about 1994.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/ford-sierra-mk1.blend. References:
# citycars/references/ford-sierra-mk1/ (gitignored). Images via Wikimedia Commons.

obj=citycar
